Oz: in first person the lightning beam ends where the middle of the view meets something, on the
crosshair. id's cgame traced it from the player's entity as the snapshots last had it (a snapshot or more
behind the view) at its eye height before the view eases up a stair, along the snapshots' aim: a step, a
hit's knockback, a jump pad or a turn swung its end off the crosshair. Damage view kick's tilt stays out
of it (cg.ozKickPitch): the shots keep going where you aimed. cg_trueLightning still sets a beam seen in
third person.

